From 1cf1034796ae94f06aab5270e089ff8c3c55792e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:50:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibCompositing: display-list damage as a region with per-run
 tags; a moved solid fill damages only what it uncovers

A tiled compositor (Chitin) rasters only the tiles damage touches, but the damage was one union rect for the whole
list: a change at the top and one at the bottom damaged everything between them, and every layer whose content
changed got all of it, whatever its own commands did. compute_display_list_damage_region returns the damage as a few
rects (merged when near, at most 16), each damaged command's rect tagged with the new list's run it belongs to (so a
layer can take only its own commands' damage), and counts of why commands were damaged.

A FillRect that only moved or resized under equal chains (same colour, op, effect; no inline clip or transform)
damages the parts of its old and new rects that do not overlap. YouTube's root background fill is the viewport at the
scroll offset when the root has no overflow rect: it moved with every scroll and damaged the whole view each frame.

compute_display_list_damage (the union) is unchanged for Ladybird's own callers.
